* /**
*  * @file GIT.CMD.FLAG
*  * @version 1.0
*  */
* CMD.FLAG(subcommand, short, long, takes-value, default, help) — declare one
* option on a subcommand.  CMD.RUN parses the sentence against the declared flags
* (via the getopt package) before dispatching, and the handler reads them back
* with GETOPT.VAL / GETOPT.HAS / GETOPT.ARG.  takes-value 0 is a boolean flag.
SUBROUTINE GIT.CMD.FLAG(GSUB, SHORT, LONG, TAKESVAL, DFLT, HELP)
COMMON /CMDPKG/ CNAME, CDESC, CSUBS, CDESCS, CHANDLERS, CFLAGS
CFLAGS<-1> = OCONV(GSUB, "MCU") : @VM : SHORT : @VM : LONG : @VM : TAKESVAL : @VM : DFLT : @VM : HELP
RETURN